# Documentation placeholder only; this is NOT a valid PEM certificate.
# Obtain the trusted database CA certificate from your database administrator.
# Save the real PEM certificate as db-ca.local.pem beside config.local.json.
# The certificate must match the CA that signs your database server certificate.
# Do not put a private key, database password, or API token in this file.
# Never disable TLS verification to work around a missing or incorrect CA.
